.09375 8.40625 42.78125 9.671875 \nQ 43.171875 9.671875 43.75 8.890625 \nQ 44.34375 8.109375 44.34375 7.71875 \nQ 44.046875 6.0625 40.71875 2.78125 \nQ 37.40625 -0.484375 34.375 -0.484375 \nQ 30.28125 -0.484375 27.734375 8.015625 \nL 25.484375 15.625 \nL 19.34375 4.984375 \nQ 16.109375 -0.59375 11.140625 -0.59375 \nQ 7.8125 -0.59375 5.46875 1.375 \nQ 4.6875 2.734375 4.6875 3.90625 \nQ 4.6875 5.375 5.703125 6.390625 \nQ 6.734375 7.421875 7.8125 7.421875 \nQ 9.078125 7.421875 10.6875 5.90625 \nQ 12.3125 4.390625 13.671875 4.390625 \nQ 14.84375 4.390625 16.3125 6.9375 \nL 24.03125 20.21875 \nL 20.015625 33.296875 \nQ 19.046875 36.625 17.390625 36.625 \nQ 15.921875 36.625 14.25 35.109375 \nQ 12.59375 33.59375 11.921875 32.328125 \nQ 11.53125 32.328125 10.9375 33.109375 \nQ 10.359375 33.890625 10.359375 34.28125 \nQ 10.640625 35.9375 13.953125 39.203125 \nQ 17.28125 42.484375 20.3125 42.484375 \nz\n\" id=\"CrimsonText-Italic-120\"></path>\n</defs>\n<g transform=\"translate(344.786011 195.265866)scale(0.2 -0.2)\">\n<use xlink:href=\"#CrimsonText-Italic-120\"></use>\n</g>\n</g>\n</g>\n<g id=\"line2d_1\">\n<path clip-path=\"url(#p2ed2c8917c)\" d=\"M 147.776574 337.721148 \nL 264.956775 44.770645 \nL 264.956775 44.770645 \n\" style=\"fill:none;stroke:#000000;stroke-linecap:square;stroke-width:2.3;\"></path>\n</g>\n<g id=\"line2d_2\">\n<path clip-path=\"url(#p2ed2c8917c)\" d=\"M 47.977168 120.928431 \nL 327.751907 120.928431 \nL 327.751907 120.928431 \n\" style=\"fill:none;stroke:#000000;stroke-linecap:square;stroke-width:2.3;\"></path>\n</g>\n</g>\n</g>\n<defs>\n<clipPath id=\"p2ed2c8917c\">\n<rect height=\"347.76\" width=\"358.531327\" x=\"7.2\" y=\"7.2\"></rect>\n</clipPath>\n</defs>\n</svg>\n<div role=\"region\" aria-label=\"Long description for graph of a system of 2 lines\" class=\"sr-only\"><ul>\n<li>For the first line in the system:<br>\n<ul>\n<li>The line is horizontal.</li>\n<li>The line passes through the following points:<br>\n<ul>\n<li>(negative 4 comma 3)</li>\n<li>(0 comma 3)</li>\n<li>(2 comma 3)</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>For the second line in the system:<br>\n<ul>\n<li>The line slants sharply up from left to right.</li>\n<li>The line passes through the following points:\n<ul>\n<li>(negative 1 comma negative 4.5)</li>\n<li>(0 comma negative 2)</li>\n<li>(2 comma 3)</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul></div></figure></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The graph of a system of linear equations is shown. What is the solution&nbsp;<math alttext=\"left parenthesis x comma y right parenthesis\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> to the system?</p>","externalid":"950dd818-fa5e-4231-b816-a13da78257e9","templateid":"42b12eed-dbb0-4c80-9cd1-94615a7f4ca2","vaultid":"9760cb42-420a-4006-b720-732a8759c67f","type":"mcq","answerOptions":[{"id":"764dbefd-6daa-4565-8196-12c16b278ed6","content":"<p><math alttext=\"left parenthesis 0 comma 3 right parenthesis\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mrow></mfenced></math></p>"},{"id":"65c4ab04-6304-49fc-b2d3-b800c8ea936b","content":"<p><math alttext=\"left parenthesis 1 comma 3 right parenthesis\"><mfenced><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mrow></mfenced></math></p>"},{"id":"2c37b29c-109c-4b6c-9b32-df29d9cd25d3","content":"<p><math alttext=\"left parenthesis 2 comma 3 right parenthesis\"><mfenced><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mrow></mfenced></math></p>"},{"id":"5587a7e2-1ef6-4d78-86ba-3f86a9c90e39","content":"<p><math alttext=\"left parenthesis 3 comma 3 right parenthesis\"><mfenced><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mrow></mfenced></math></p>"}],"correct_answer":["C"]},"createDate":1691007959818,"updateDate":1691007959818}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959818, 1691007959818),
    ($SATQ$b23bba4c$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$025553-DC$SATQ$, $SATQ$disclosed$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Algebra$SATQ$, $SATQ$H$SATQ$, $SATQ$H.C.$SATQ$, $SATQ$Linear equations in two variables$SATQ$, $SATQ$E$SATQ$, 1, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, $SATQ$<div class="stimulus_reference " xmlns="http://www.imsglobal.org/xsd/apip/apipv1p0/qtiitem/imsqti_v2p1"><p class="standalone_statement style:1 "><span class="math_expression "><span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/b23bba4c/img_000_0e7a9199.png" alt="3 a plus 4 b, equals 25"></span></span></p></div>
$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p class="stem_paragraph ">A shipping company charged a customer $25 to ship some small boxes and some large boxes. The equation above represents the relationship between <span class="italic">a</span>, the number of small boxes, and <span class="italic">b</span>, the number of large boxes, the customer had shipped. If the customer had 3 small boxes shipped, how many large boxes were shipped?</p>
$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"a","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">3</p>\n"},{"id":"b","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">4</p>\n"},{"id":"c","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">5</p>\n"},{"id":"d","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">6</p>\n"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["B"]$SATQ$::jsonb, NULL, $SATQ$<p>Choice B is correct. It&rsquo;s given that <span class="italic">a</span> represents the number of small boxes and <span class="italic">b</span> represents the number of large boxes the customer had shipped. If the customer had 3 small boxes shipped, then <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/b23bba4c/img_001_6d1e45fb.png" alt="a, equals 3"></span>. Substituting 3 for <span class="italic">a</span> in the equation <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/b23bba4c/img_002_0e7a9199.png" alt="3 a, plus 4 b, equals 25"></span> yields <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/b23bba4c/img_003_a89ecf2b.png" alt="3 times 3, plus 4 b, equals 25"></span> or <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/b23bba4c/img_004_3a138243.png" alt="9 plus 4 b, equals 25"></span>. Subtracting 9 from both sides of the equation yields <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/b23bba4c/img_005_af9ee16e.png" alt="4 b equals 16"></span>. Dividing both sides of this equation by 4 yields <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/b23bba4c/img_006_5e23e36f.png" alt="b equals 4"></span>. Therefore, the customer had 4 large boxes shipped.<p>Choices A, C, and D are incorrect. If the number of large boxes shipped is 3, then <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/b23bba4c/img_007_8f292e98.png" alt="b equals 3"></span>. Substituting 3 for <span class="italic">b</span> in the given equation yields <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/b23bba4c/img_008_6ef0d443.png" alt="3 a, plus, 4 times 3, equals 25"></span> or <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/b23bba4c/img_009_7f8693a5.png" alt="3 a, plus 12, equals 25"></span>. Subtracting 12 from both sides of the equation and then dividing by 3 yields <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/b23bba4c/img_010_3998dd8c.png" alt="a, equals thirteen thirds"></span>. However, it&rsquo;s given that the number of small boxes shipped, <span class="italic">a</span>, is 3, not <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/b23bba4c/img_011_5ad404f0.png" alt="thirteen thirds"></span>, so <span class="italic">b</span> cannot equal 3. Similarly, if <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/b23bba4c/img_012_a2863d96.png" alt="b equals 5"></span> or <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/b23bba4c/img_013_0a006f13.png" alt="b equals 6"></span>, then <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/b23bba4c/img_014_00efa601.png" alt="a, equals five thirds"></span> or <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/b23bba4c/img_015_c21ac0a0.png" alt="a, equals one third"></span>, respectively, which is also not true.</p><p>&nbsp;</p></p>
$SATQ$, false, 16, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$Multiple Choice$SATQ$, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ${"questionId":"b23bba4c","external_id":null,"disclosed_item_id":"025553-DC","source":"disclosed","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"H","domain":"Algebra","skill_cd":"H.C.","skill_desc":"Linear equations in two variables","difficulty":"E","score_band_range_cd":1,"type":"mcq","stimulus":"<div class=\"stimulus_reference \" xmlns=\"http://www.imsglobal.org/xsd/apip/apipv1p0/qtiitem/imsqti_v2p1\"><p class=\"standalone_statement style:1 \"><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/b23bba4c/img_000_0e7a9199.png\" alt=\"3 a plus 4 b, equals 25\"></span></span></p></div>\n","stem":"<p class=\"stem_paragraph \">A shipping company charged a customer $25 to ship some small boxes and some large boxes. The equation above represents the relationship between <span class=\"italic\">a</span>, the number of small boxes, and <span class=\"italic\">b</span>, the number of large boxes, the customer had shipped. If the customer had 3 small boxes shipped, how many large boxes were shipped?</p>\n","answerOptions":[{"id":"a","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">3</p>\n"},{"id":"b","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">4</p>\n"},{"id":"c","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">5</p>\n"},{"id":"d","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">6</p>\n"}],"keys":null,"correct_answer":["B"],"rationale":"<p>Choice B is correct. It&rsquo;s given that <span class=\"italic\">a</span> represents the number of small boxes and <span class=\"italic\">b</span> represents the number of large boxes the customer had shipped. If the customer had 3 small boxes shipped, then <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/b23bba4c/img_001_6d1e45fb.png\" alt=\"a, equals 3\"></span>. Substituting 3 for <span class=\"italic\">a</span> in the equation <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/b23bba4c/img_002_0e7a9199.png\" alt=\"3 a, plus 4 b, equals 25\"></span> yields <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/b23bba4c/img_003_a89ecf2b.png\" alt=\"3 times 3, plus 4 b, equals 25\"></span> or <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/b23bba4c/img_004_3a138243.png\" alt=\"9 plus 4 b, equals 25\"></span>. Subtracting 9 from both sides of the equation yields <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/b23bba4c/img_005_af9ee16e.png\" alt=\"4 b equals 16\"></span>. Dividing both sides of this equation by 4 yields <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/b23bba4c/img_006_5e23e36f.png\" alt=\"b equals 4\"></span>. Therefore, the customer had 4 large boxes shipped.<p>Choices A, C, and D are incorrect. If the number of large boxes shipped is 3, then <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/b23bba4c/img_007_8f292e98.png\" alt=\"b equals 3\"></span>. Substituting 3 for <span class=\"italic\">b</span> in the given equation yields <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/b23bba4c/img_008_6ef0d443.png\" alt=\"3 a, plus, 4 times 3, equals 25\"></span> or <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/b23bba4c/img_009_7f8693a5.png\" alt=\"3 a, plus 12, equals 25\"></span>. Subtracting 12 from both sides of the equation and then dividing by 3 yields <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/b23bba4c/img_010_3998dd8c.png\" alt=\"a, equals thirteen thirds\"></span>. However, it&rsquo;s given that the number of small boxes shipped, <span class=\"italic\">a</span>, is 3, not <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/b23bba4c/img_011_5ad404f0.png\" alt=\"thirteen thirds\"></span>, so <span class=\"italic\">b</span> cannot equal 3. Similarly, if <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/b23bba4c/img_012_a2863d96.png\" alt=\"b equals 5\"></span> or <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/b23bba4c/img_013_0a006f13.png\" alt=\"b equals 6\"></span>, then <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/b23bba4c/img_014_00efa601.png\" alt=\"a, equals five thirds\"></span> or <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/b23bba4c/img_015_c21ac0a0.png\" alt=\"a, equals one third\"></span>, respectively, which is also not true.</p><p>&nbsp;</p></p>\n","answer_style":"Multiple Choice","section":"Math","image_count":16,"raw_list":{"updateDate":1691007959619,"pPcc":"SAT#H","questionId":"b23bba4c","skill_cd":"H.C.","score_band_range_cd":1,"skill_desc":"Linear equations in two variables","createDate":1691007959619,"program":"SAT","primary_class_cd_desc":"Algebra","ibn":"025553-DC","external_id":null,"primary_class_cd":"H","uId":"2bdce850-ca35-4d06-b3d3-214d7034503b","difficulty":"E"},"raw_detail":{"item_id":"025553-DC","section":"Math","body":"<div class=\"stimulus_reference \" xmlns=\"http://www.imsglobal.org/xsd/apip/apipv1p0/qtiitem/imsqti_v2p1\"><p class=\"standalone_statement style:1 \"><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"3 a plus 4 b, equals 25\"></span></span></p></div>\n","prompt":"<p class=\"stem_paragraph \">A shipping company charged a customer $25 to ship some small boxes and some large boxes. The equation above represents the relationship between <span class=\"italic\">a</span>, the number of small boxes, and <span class=\"italic\">b</span>, the number of large boxes, the customer had shipped. If the customer had 3 small boxes shipped, how many large boxes were shipped?</p>\n","answer":{"style":"Multiple Choice","choices":{"a":{"body":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">3</p>\n"},"b":{"body":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">4</p>\n"},"c":{"body":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">5</p>\n"},"d":{"body":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">6</p>\n"}},"correct_choice":"b","rationale":"<p>Choice B is correct. It&rsquo;s given that <span class=\"italic\">a</span> represents the number of small boxes and <span class=\"italic\">b</span> represents the number of large boxes the customer had shipped. If the customer had 3 small boxes shipped, then <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"a, equals 3\"></span>. Substituting 3 for <span class=\"italic\">a</span> in the equation <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"3 a, plus 4 b, equals 25\"></span> yields <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"3 times 3, plus 4 b, equals 25\"></span> or <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"9 plus 4 b, equals 25\"></span>. Subtracting 9 from both sides of the equation yields <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"4 b equals 16\"></span>. Dividing both sides of this equation by 4 yields <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"b equals 4\"></span>. Therefore, the customer had 4 large boxes shipped.<p>Choices A, C, and D are incorrect. If the number of large boxes shipped is 3, then <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"b equals 3\"></span>. Substituting 3 for <span class=\"italic\">b</span> in the given equation yields <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"3 a, plus, 4 times 3, equals 25\"></span> or <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"3 a, plus 12, equals 25\"></span>. Subtracting 12 from both sides of the equation and then dividing by 3 yields <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"a, equals thirteen thirds\"></span>. However, it&rsquo;s given that the number of small boxes shipped, <span class=\"italic\">a</span>, is 3, not <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"thirteen thirds\"></span>, so <span class=\"italic\">b</span> cannot equal 3. Similarly, if <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"b equals 5\"></span> or <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"b equals 6\"></span>, then <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"a, equals five thirds\"></span> or <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"a, equals one third\"></span>, respectively, which is also not true.</p><p>&nbsp;</p></p>\n"}},"createDate":1691007959619,"updateDate":1691007959619}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959619, 1691007959619),
