7/img_007_5754dfab.png\" alt=\"0 point 5 is less than or equal to p, which is less than or equal to 0 point 8 5\"></span>. When <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/b31c3117/img_008_4ac18373.png\" alt=\"p equals 0 point 5\"></span>, <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/b31c3117/img_009_583c1487.png\" alt=\"H equals, 120 times 0 point 5, plus 60\"></span>, or <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/b31c3117/img_010_123a8f4e.png\" alt=\"H equals 120\"></span>. When <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/b31c3117/img_011_de8ff9e9.png\" alt=\"p equals 0 point 8 5\"></span>, <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/b31c3117/img_012_3d737e23.png\" alt=\"H equals, 120 times 0 point 8 5, plus, 60\"></span>, or <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/b31c3117/img_013_38f8b9b1.png\" alt=\"H equals 162\"></span>. Therefore, the inequality that describes Alice&rsquo;s target training heart rate is <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/b31c3117/img_014_dc05db1a.png\" alt=\"120 is less than or equal to H, which is less than or equal to 162\"></span>.<p>Choice B is incorrect. This inequality describes Alice&rsquo;s target heart rate for <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/b31c3117/img_015_6a8ff226.png\" alt=\"0 point 3 5 is less than or equal to p, which is less than or equal to 0 point 5\"></span>. Choice C is incorrect. This inequality describes her target heart rate for <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/b31c3117/img_016_f07680a1.png\" alt=\"0 is less than or equal to p, which is less than or equal to 0 point 8 5\"></span>. Choice D is incorrect. This inequality describes&nbsp; her target heart rate for <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/b31c3117/img_017_d0b1696e.png\" alt=\"0 is less than or equal to p, which is less than or equal to 0 point 3 5\"></span>.</p><p>&nbsp;</p></p>\n","answer_style":"Multiple Choice","section":"Math","image_count":18,"raw_list":{"updateDate":1691007959622,"pPcc":"SAT#H","questionId":"b31c3117","skill_cd":"H.E.","score_band_range_cd":4,"skill_desc":"Linear inequalities in one or two variables","createDate":1691007959622,"program":"SAT","primary_class_cd_desc":"Algebra","ibn":"028867-DC","external_id":null,"primary_class_cd":"H","uId":"713d1d26-6cd4-4fca-aed0-d7d29313edf5","difficulty":"M"},"raw_detail":{"item_id":"028867-DC","section":"Math","body":"<div class=\"stimulus_reference \" xmlns=\"http://www.imsglobal.org/xsd/apip/apipv1p0/qtiitem/imsqti_v2p1\"><p class=\"standalone_statement style:1 \"><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"H equals, 120 p, plus 60\"></span></span></p></div>\n","prompt":"<p class=\"stem_paragraph \">The Karvonen formula above shows the relationship between Alice&rsquo;s target heart rate <span class=\"italic\">H</span>, in beats per minute (bpm), and the intensity level <span class=\"italic\">p</span> of different activities. When <span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"p equals 0\"></span></span>, Alice has a resting heart rate. When <span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"p equals 1\"></span></span>, Alice has her maximum heart rate. It is recommended that <span class=\"italic\">p</span> be between 0.5 and 0.85 for Alice when she trains. Which of the following inequalities describes Alice&rsquo;s target training heart rate?</p>\n","answer":{"style":"Multiple Choice","choices":{"a":{"body":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \"><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"120 is less than or equal to H, which is less than or equal to 162\"></span></span></p>\n"},"b":{"body":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \"><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"102 is less than or equal to H, which is less than or equal to 120\"></span></span></p>\n"},"c":{"body":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \"><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"60 is less than or equal to H, which is less than or equal to 162\"></span></span></p>\n"},"d":{"body":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \"><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"60 is less than or equal to H, which is less than or equal to 102\"></span></span></p>\n"}},"correct_choice":"a","rationale":"<p>Choice A is correct. When Alice trains, it&rsquo;s recommended that <span class=\"italic\">p</span> be between 0.5 and 0.85. Therefore, her target training heart rate is represented by the values of <span class=\"italic\">H</span> corresponding to <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"0 point 5 is less than or equal to p, which is less than or equal to 0 point 8 5\"></span>. When <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"p equals 0 point 5\"></span>, <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"H equals, 120 times 0 point 5, plus 60\"></span>, or <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"H equals 120\"></span>. When <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"p equals 0 point 8 5\"></span>, <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"H equals, 120 times 0 point 8 5, plus, 60\"></span>, or <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"H equals 162\"></span>. Therefore, the inequality that describes Alice&rsquo;s target training heart rate is <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"120 is less than or equal to H, which is less than or equal to 162\"></span>.<p>Choice B is incorrect. This inequality describes Alice&rsquo;s target heart rate for <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"0 point 3 5 is less than or equal to p, which is less than or equal to 0 point 5\"></span>. Choice C is incorrect. This inequality describes her target heart rate for <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"0 is less than or equal to p, which is less than or equal to 0 point 8 5\"></span>. Choice D is incorrect. This inequality describes&nbsp; her target heart rate for <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"0 is less than or equal to p, which is less than or equal to 0 point 3 5\"></span>.</p><p>&nbsp;</p></p>\n"}},"createDate":1691007959622,"updateDate":1691007959622}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959622, 1691007959622),
    ($SATQ$b3abf40f$SATQ$, $SATQ$ea18109c-11ea-4e1e-a907-b4a77b4a93e1$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$ea7edb73-7cc2-49de-8d7d-2072f97d796f$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Algebra$SATQ$, $SATQ$H$SATQ$, $SATQ$H.B.$SATQ$, $SATQ$Linear functions$SATQ$, $SATQ$H$SATQ$, 6, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: center;"><math alttext="upper F left parenthesis x right parenthesis equals nine fifths left parenthesis x minus 273.15 right parenthesis plus 32"><mi>F</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>9</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>273.15</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mn>32</mn></math></p>
