    ($SATQ$b52e5b6f$SATQ$, $SATQ$db170278-9037-413e-b5e2-ed81bbf21899$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Algebra$SATQ$, $SATQ$H$SATQ$, $SATQ$H.C.$SATQ$, $SATQ$Linear equations in two variables$SATQ$, $SATQ$E$SATQ$, 1, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">A mixture consisting of only vitamin D and calcium has a total mass of <math alttext="150"><mn>150</mn>
</math> grams. The mass of vitamin D in the mixture is <math alttext="50"><mn>50</mn>
</math> grams. What is the mass, in grams, of calcium in the mixture?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"e31ac9d5-7783-4928-851d-2a48941c71ba","content":"<p><math alttext=\"200\"><mn>200</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"da34dc6d-d6b1-434f-a9a3-f5407b353db1","content":"<p><math alttext=\"150\"><mn>150</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"9ee6a37b-74f0-45d9-b7e3-2afda52e2496","content":"<p><math alttext=\"100\"><mn>100</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"9eb9cc9f-42d2-4d54-8c57-d55e25e58a4d","content":"<p><math alttext=\"50\"><mn>50</mn>\n</math></p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["C"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["9ee6a37b-74f0-45d9-b7e3-2afda52e2496"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice C is correct. Let <math alttext="d"><mi>d</mi>
</math> represent the mass, in grams, of vitamin D in the mixture, and let <math alttext="c"><mi>c</mi>
</math> represent the mass, in grams, of calcium in the mixture. It&rsquo;s given that the mixture consists of only vitamin D and calcium and that the total mass of the mixture is <math alttext="150"><mn>150</mn>
</math> grams. Therefore, the equation <math alttext="d plus c equals 150"><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>150</mn></math> represents this situation. It&rsquo;s also given that the mass of vitamin D in the mixture is <math alttext="50"><mn>50</mn>
</math> grams. Substituting <math alttext="50"><mn>50</mn>
</math> for <math alttext="d"><mi>d</mi>
</math> in the equation <math alttext="d plus c equals 150"><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>150</mn></math> yields <math alttext="50 plus c equals 150"><mn>50</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>150</mn></math>. Subtracting <math alttext="50"><mn>50</mn>
</math> from both sides of this equation yields <math alttext="c equals 100"><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn></math>. Therefore, the mass of calcium in the mixture is <math alttext="100"><mn>100</mn>
</math> grams.</p>
<p>Choice A is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>
<p>Choice B is incorrect. This is the total mass, in grams, of the mixture, not the mass, in grams, of calcium in the mixture.</p>
<p>Choice D is incorrect. This is the mass, in grams, of vitamin D in the mixture, not the mass, in grams, of calcium in the mixture.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"b52e5b6f","external_id":"db170278-9037-413e-b5e2-ed81bbf21899","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":null,"uId":"1e9fce2b-17e3-40b2-aeda-e6bfc46d489a","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"H","domain":"Algebra","skill_cd":"H.C.","skill_desc":"Linear equations in two variables","difficulty":"E","score_band_range_cd":1,"type":"mcq","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">A mixture consisting of only vitamin D and calcium has a total mass of <math alttext=\"150\"><mn>150</mn>\n</math> grams. The mass of vitamin D in the mixture is <math alttext=\"50\"><mn>50</mn>\n</math> grams. What is the mass, in grams, of calcium in the mixture?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"e31ac9d5-7783-4928-851d-2a48941c71ba","content":"<p><math alttext=\"200\"><mn>200</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"da34dc6d-d6b1-434f-a9a3-f5407b353db1","content":"<p><math alttext=\"150\"><mn>150</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"9ee6a37b-74f0-45d9-b7e3-2afda52e2496","content":"<p><math alttext=\"100\"><mn>100</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"9eb9cc9f-42d2-4d54-8c57-d55e25e58a4d","content":"<p><math alttext=\"50\"><mn>50</mn>\n</math></p>"}],"keys":["9ee6a37b-74f0-45d9-b7e3-2afda52e2496"],"correct_answer":["C"],"rationale":"<p>Choice C is correct. Let <math alttext=\"d\"><mi>d</mi>\n</math> represent the mass, in grams, of vitamin D in the mixture, and let <math alttext=\"c\"><mi>c</mi>\n</math> represent the mass, in grams, of calcium in the mixture. It&rsquo;s given that the mixture consists of only vitamin D and calcium and that the total mass of the mixture is <math alttext=\"150\"><mn>150</mn>\n</math> grams. Therefore, the equation <math alttext=\"d plus c equals 150\"><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>150</mn></math> represents this situation. It&rsquo;s also given that the mass of vitamin D in the mixture is <math alttext=\"50\"><mn>50</mn>\n</math> grams. Substituting <math alttext=\"50\"><mn>50</mn>\n</math> for <math alttext=\"d\"><mi>d</mi>\n</math> in the equation <math alttext=\"d plus c equals 150\"><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>150</mn></math> yields <math alttext=\"50 plus c equals 150\"><mn>50</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>150</mn></math>. Subtracting <math alttext=\"50\"><mn>50</mn>\n</math> from both sides of this equation yields <math alttext=\"c equals 100\"><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn></math>. Therefore, the mass of calcium in the mixture is <math alttext=\"100\"><mn>100</mn>\n</math> grams.</p>\n<p>Choice A is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>\n<p>Choice B is incorrect. This is the total mass, in grams, of the mixture, not the mass, in grams, of calcium in the mixture.</p>\n<p>Choice D is incorrect. This is the mass, in grams, of vitamin D in the mixture, not the mass, in grams, of calcium in the mixture.</p>","parenttemplatename":null,"parenttemplateid":null,"templateclusterid":null,"templateclustername":null,"origin":null,"position":null,"image_count":0,"raw_list":{"updateDate":1730147357390,"pPcc":"SAT#H","questionId":"b52e5b6f","skill_cd":"H.C.","score_band_range_cd":1,"skill_desc":"Linear equations in two variables","createDate":1730147357390,"program":"SAT","primary_class_cd_desc":"Algebra","ibn":"","external_id":"db170278-9037-413e-b5e2-ed81bbf21899","primary_class_cd":"H","uId":"1e9fce2b-17e3-40b2-aeda-e6bfc46d489a","difficulty":"E"},"raw_detail":{"answerOptions":[{"content":"<p><math alttext=\"200\"><mn>200</mn>\n</math></p>","id":"e31ac9d5-7783-4928-851d-2a48941c71ba"},{"content":"<p><math alttext=\"150\"><mn>150</mn>\n</math></p>","id":"da34dc6d-d6b1-434f-a9a3-f5407b353db1"},{"content":"<p><math alttext=\"100\"><mn>100</mn>\n</math></p>","id":"9ee6a37b-74f0-45d9-b7e3-2afda52e2496"},{"content":"<p><math a