 class=\"italic\">x</span> = 7.</p></p>\n","answer_style":"SPR","section":"Math","image_count":3,"raw_list":{"updateDate":1691007959619,"pPcc":"SAT#H","questionId":"b544a348","skill_cd":"H.D.","score_band_range_cd":5,"skill_desc":"Systems of two linear equations in two variables","createDate":1691007959619,"program":"SAT","primary_class_cd_desc":"Algebra","ibn":"025580-DC","external_id":null,"primary_class_cd":"H","uId":"e6786e0f-4547-430c-acad-1a8fe2cab840","difficulty":"M"},"raw_detail":{"item_id":"025580-DC","section":"Math","body":"<div class=\"stimulus_reference \" xmlns=\"http://www.imsglobal.org/xsd/apip/apipv1p0/qtiitem/imsqti_v2p1\"><p class=\"standalone_statement style:1 \"><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"Equation 1: 5 x plus 3 y, equals 38; Equation 2: x plus 3 y, equals 10\n\"></span></span></p></div>\n","prompt":"<p class=\"stem_paragraph \">In the solution <span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"x comma y\"></span></span> to the system of equations above, what is the value of <span class=\"italic\">x</span> ?</p>\n","answer":{"style":"SPR","rationale":"<p>The correct answer is 7. Subtracting the second equation from the first equation eliminates the variable <span class=\"italic\">y</span>.<p><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"Equation 1, 5 x, plus 3 y, equals 38; Equation 2,  x plus 3 y, equals 10; Subtracting equation 2 from equation 1 yields equation 3, which is 4 x, equals 28.\"></span></p><p>Dividing both sides of the resulting equation by 4 yields <span class=\"italic\">x</span> = 7.</p></p>\n"}},"createDate":1691007959619,"updateDate":1691007959619,"correct_answer_extracted_from_rationale":true}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959619,